Reindexing a computable presentation along a primitive-recursive involution enumerates the same neighbourhoods in the permuted order. Surjectivity takes a preimage index and applies the involution, which cancels. The intersection and consistency deciders transfer by composition with the primitive-recursive maps that apply the involution to the components of a triple code and of a pair code; one direction of consistency renames the witness by the involution, and the other cancels a second application. The intersection operation and the master index are transported in the same way. Primitive recursiveness of the new intersection is composition with the pairwise reindexing, and its specification cancels one application before invoking the original specification on the renamed witness.
